    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a concentrated attack, led by **Jackson Merrill**, who anchors the lineup with an elite score of 66.54. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a high-leverage spot in the two-hole against a mid-tier arm in May (xERA 3.99); the combination of a favorable platoon advantage and his prime lineup positioning makes him our most bankable asset for offensive production. Conversely, our top-of-order anchor **Drake Baldwin** faces a tougher test against Yamamoto (xERA 3.40). While **Drake Baldwin** holds a solid 50.52 score, his lead-off utility is somewhat mitigated by the elite skill of the opposing starter, necessitating a reliance on volume rather than pure matchup dominance to deliver efficiency.\n\nThe outfield corner presents a distinct challenge as both **Kyle Tucker** and **Andy Pages** contend with Sale (xERA 2.79). **Kyle Tucker** (47.59) remains in the lineup despite the challenging left-on-left matchup, primarily because his raw talent floor remains too high to bench, even with an uncharacteristic eighth-spot placement. **Andy Pages** (43.88) rounds out the daily outfield rotation; while his projection is dampened by the SP skill level, his neutral platoon status keeps him marginally above our bench threshold. Given the scarcity of stolen bases, we continue to monitor the utility of **Nasim Nunez** and **Brayan Rocchio** on the periphery, though they remain on the bench today as the core starters offer a superior blend of projected runs and RBI. \n\nThe most notable bench decision involved keeping high-ceiling assets inactive due to today\u2019s schedule gaps, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Gunnar Henderson** absent due to team off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** currently sidelined on the IL, our depth is thinner than usual, placing extra pressure on **Heliot Ramos** and **Coby Mayo** to stay ready should lineups shift before first pitch. We are currently navigating a \"wait and see\" approach regarding weather, but no specific risks have been flagged to pull **Kyle Tucker** or **Andy Pages** from the start; we will prioritize preserving game caps for our top producers while ensuring **Jackson Merrill** receives maximum exposure today.",
